"""Independent 2038/N and 2042/A-D solutions."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
ANSWERS=[
('2038/N','Keep the two digits and replace only the comparison character with their true comparison. If already true zero edits; otherwise at least one edit is necessary and this uses one. O(1) per case.',r'''#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;int main(){int t;cin>>t;while(t--){string s;cin>>s;s[1]=s[0]<s[2]?'<':s[0]>s[2]?'>':'=';cout<<s<<'\n';}}'''),
('2042/A','Sort descending and take the longest original prefix with sum S<=k. If S=k no additions. Otherwise add k-S to the largest chest in that prefix (or the largest chest overall if prefix empty). The selected prefix then totals k and still dominates later chests. Any valid set selected by greediness must contain at least the largest original chests until its total reaches k, so cannot preserve more original coins than this prefix. Answer k-S. O(n log n) time, O(n) space.',r'''#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;int main(){int t;cin>>t;while(t--){int n,k;cin>>n>>k;vector<int>a(n);for(int&x:a)cin>>x;sort(a.rbegin(),a.rend());int s=0;for(int x:a){if(s+x>k)break;s+=x;}cout<<k-s<<'\n';}}'''),
('2042/B','Let s colors occur once and d colors occur at least twice. Singleton colors are worth two points to Alice, and optimal alternating claims give her ceil(s/2). For every repeated color Alice can guarantee at least one point by claiming a first marble when threatened; Bob can prevent a second point by responding in that color. Pairing responses yields exactly d additional points, independent of repeated multiplicities. Thus answer 2*ceil(s/2)+d. O(n) time and space.',r'''#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;int main(){int t;cin>>t;while(t--){int n;cin>>n;vector<int>f(n+1);for(int i=0,x;i<n;i++){cin>>x;f[x]++;}int s=0,d=0;for(int x:f){s+=x==1;d+=x>1;}cout<<2*((s+1)/2)+d<<'\n';}}'''),
('2042/C','Every boundary increases all subsequent fish values by one, so contributes suffix (number of ones minus zeros) to Bob minus Alice. Boundaries contribute independently. Sort all n-1 suffix contributions descending and take the shortest prefix whose sum reaches k; its size plus one is the minimum groups. If all positive contributions cannot reach k output -1. O(n log n) time, O(n) space.',r'''#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;int main(){ios::sync_with_stdio(false);cin.tie(nullptr);int t;cin>>t;while(t--){int n;long long k;string s;cin>>n>>k>>s;vector<int>v;int sum=0;for(int i=n-1;i>=1;i--){sum+=s[i]=='1'?1:-1;v.push_back(sum);}sort(v.rbegin(),v.rend());long long score=0;int ans=-1;for(int i=0;i<(int)v.size();i++){score+=v[i];if(score>=k){ans=i+2;break;}}cout<<ans<<'\n';}}'''),
('2042/D','Sort by l ascending then r descending. All strict containing intervals then occur earlier. Among earlier intervals with right>=r, their intersection has left equal to maximum l and right equal to minimum r. Find minimum r with an ordered set lower_bound, and maximum l with a Fenwick maximum indexed by reversed compressed right coordinates. The recommendation count is l-maxLeft+minRight-r. If there are duplicate identical intervals, each has a predictor with exactly the same range, forcing zero; handle by frequency. O(n log n) time, O(n) space.',r'''#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;struct Node{int l,r,id;};int main(){ios::sync_with_stdio(false);cin.tie(nullptr);int t;cin>>t;while(t--){int n;cin>>n;vector<Node>a(n);vector<int>vals;map<pair<int,int>,int>freq;for(int i=0;i<n;i++){cin>>a[i].l>>a[i].r;a[i].id=i;vals.push_back(a[i].r);freq[{a[i].l,a[i].r}]++;}sort(vals.begin(),vals.end());vals.erase(unique(vals.begin(),vals.end()),vals.end());sort(a.begin(),a.end(),[](Node x,Node y){return x.l!=y.l?x.l<y.l:x.r>y.r;});vector<int>bit(vals.size()+1);vector<long long>ans(n);set<int>rights;for(auto x:a){int at=vals.size()-(lower_bound(vals.begin(),vals.end(),x.r)-vals.begin());int mx=0;for(int p=at;p;p-=p&-p)mx=max(mx,bit[p]);auto it=rights.lower_bound(x.r);if(freq[{x.l,x.r}]==1&&it!=rights.end())ans[x.id]=1LL*x.l-mx+*it-x.r;rights.insert(x.r);for(int p=at;p<(int)bit.size();p+=p&-p)bit[p]=max(bit[p],x.l);}for(auto x:ans)cout<<x<<'\n';}}''')]
if __name__=='__main__':
    p=Path('backend/data/bench/codeforces700_20261116/assistant_answers_v1/shard_test_000_199.jsonl')
    with p.open('a',encoding='utf-8') as out:
        for ident,explanation,code in ANSWERS:
            out.write(json.dumps({'id':ident,'split':'test','author':'current chat assistant','status':'authored','explanation':explanation,'cpp_code':code,'validation':'not executed'})+'\n')
